At Sat, 18 Aug 2007 15:33:27 +0200,
Daniel Persch wrote:
> 
> Dear Developers,
> 
> I'm using the on-board AC97 in 6-channel mode with analog output.
> However everything works fine except front channels:
> 
> - front right is playing front left
> - front left is mute
> 
> In stereo mode:
> 
> - front right is playing front left
> - center is playing front right
> 
> I was wandering whether someone could tell me where in the source I can
> play with the channel-settings/slots or if there is a solution for my
> issue.

VIA82xx is known to work, so far, unless it's an unknown incompatible
device (that I don't think of).  Maybe the problem is rather the codec
initialization.  Which codec chip is on it?  You can see the
information in /proc/asound/card0/codec97#*/* files.


Takashi
